{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37"],"question":"entry-3581463689 OTelConf RC support PR merge as is normal review release blocked","page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false,"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]}},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-07]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-26\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3581463689  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-26T14:02:28Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-26T16:36:01Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-11-20  \\n\\n## Attendees\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn  \\n\\n- Owen Williams  \\n\\n- Sam Xie\\n\\n- Alex Boten  \\n\\n- David Ashpole  \\n\\n- Bryan Boreham  \\n\\n- (Mentioned: Robert Pająk)\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-07]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-26\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3581463689  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-26T14:02:28Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-26T16:36:01Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-11-20  \\n\\n## Discussions\\n\\n### 1. Next Go release & OTelConf RC support\\n\\n- Release blocked on RC support module; PR needs reviews.\\n\\n- Requested changes from Alex do not need to be in the current PR.\\n\\n- Module is `0.x`; breaking changes acceptable later.\\n\\n- Avoid exposing public API known to be removed immediately.\\n\\n- Discussed handling experimental features:\\n\\n  - `WithExperimentalFeatures`-style flag likely unhelpful.\\n\\n  - Possible `x` submodule to clearly isolate experimental APIs.\\n\\n  - Aligns with OTel-wide push for opt-in experimental features.\\n\\n### 2. HTTP default client deprecation (OTel HTTP)\\n\\n- Work deprecating default HTTP client usage is in progress.\\n\\n- `POST`/`GET` helpers rely on `http.DefaultClient` and limit configurability.\\n\\n- Follow-up PRs exist; need review for inclusion in upcoming release.\\n\\n### 3. Observability work & non-blocking PRs\\n\\n- Several observability PRs (e.g., self-observability for OTel gRPC) are ongoing, not release-blocking.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 07 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 26 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3581463689 author pellar creat 2025 11 26t14 02 28z updat 2025 11 26t16 36 01z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 11 20 attende tyler yahn owen william sam xie alex boten david ashpol bryan boreham mention robert paj ą k sourc id src note 07 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 26 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3581463689 author pellar creat 2025 11 26t14 02 28z updat 2025 11 26t16 36 01z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 11 20 discuss 1 next go releas otelconf rc support releas block on rc support modul pr need review request chang from alex do not need to be in the current pr modul is 0 x break chang accept later avoid expos public api known to be remov immedi discuss handl experiment featur withexperimentalfeatur style flag like unhelp possibl x submodul to clear isol experiment api align with otel wide push for opt in experiment featur 2 http default client deprec otel http work deprec default http client usag is in progress post get helper reli on http defaultcli and limit configur follow up pr exist need review for inclus in upcom releas 3 observ work non block pr sever observ pr e g self observ for otel grpc are ongo not releas block\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"0740d1ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"id\": \"c5a65f87687b3520\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3402275071829607, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1671563702613725, \"vector_similarity\": 0.74406016, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"0740d1ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 3959, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:18\", \"token_count\": 1379, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- Two non-observability items noted:\\n\\n  - Sync map / atomics for fixed bucket histograms.\\n\\n  - Exemplar reservoir changes.\\n\\n- Safe to slip to next release; include if ready.\\n\\n### 4. Stabilizing new attribute value types\\n\\n- Discussion about stabilizing new spec attribute types (byte arrays, “any” type).\\n\\n- Prototype implementation exists and needs review.\\n\\n- Considered tricky; careful review needed around limits and types.\\n\\n### 5. Processor `Enabled` method\\n\\n- Proposal from Robert to move `Enabled` from filter processor to main processor interface.\\n\\n- Spec now stabilized and allows this.\\n\\n- Pros: consistent API, less ad-hoc type assertion/boilerplate in docs.\\n\\n- Con: processors that are “always enabled” need a trivial `Enabled() bool { return true }`.\\n\\n- General agreement; will revisit for final confirmation.\\n\\n### 6. OTLP `insecure` support (logs, env vars, spec)\\n\\n- PR adds `insecure` (env var) support for OTLP **logs**, matching traces/metrics.\\n\\n- HTTP OTLP config historically messy; env vars common in practice.\\n\\n- Spec unclear due to moratorium on env vars.\\n\\n- Direction: add logs support in Go; push for spec clarity later.\\n\\n### 7. Collector protobuf changes & PDataGen\\n\\n- Collector removed dependency on Go protobuf types; now uses `pdataGen`.\\n\\n- Large internal rewrite; significant line count reduction.\\n\\n- Benchmarks improved (fewer allocations).\\n\\n- Some cross-language quirks surfaced but manageable.\\n\\n- Go SIG interested in exploring similar approaches; needs more benchmarking.\\n\\n### 8. KubeCon & talks\\n\\n- First SIG meeting since KubeCon.\\n\\n- Members encouraged to share notable talks and videos once available.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-07]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-26\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3581463689  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-26T14:02:28Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-26T16:36:01Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-11-20  \\n\\n## Decisions\\n\\n- Merge OTelConf RC support PR as-is (pending normal review).\\n\\n- Track experimental API structure review (e.g., `x` submodule) under the `1.40.0` milestone.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"two non observ item note sync map atom for fix bucket histogram exemplar reservoir chang safe to slip to next releas includ if readi 4 stabil new attribut valu type discuss about stabil new spec attribut type byte array ani type prototyp implement exist and need review consid tricki care review need around limit and type 5 processor enabl method propos from robert to move enabl from filter processor to main processor interfac spec now stabil and allow this pro consist api less ad hoc type assert boilerpl in doc con processor that are alway enabl need a trivial enabl bool return true general agreement will revisit for final confirm 6 otlp insecur support log env var spec pr add insecur env var support for otlp log match trace metric http otlp config histor messi env var common in practic spec unclear due to moratorium on env var direct add log support in go push for spec clariti later 7 collector protobuf chang pdatagen collector remov depend on go protobuf type now us pdatagen larg intern rewrit signific line count reduct benchmark improv fewer alloc some cross languag quirk surfac but manag go sig interest in explor similar approach need more benchmark 8 kubecon talk first sig meet sinc kubecon member encourag to share notabl talk and video onc avail sourc id src note 07 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 26 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3581463689 author pellar creat 2025 11 26t14 02 28z updat 2025 11 26t16 36 01z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 11 20 decis merg otelconf rc support pr ais pend normal review track experiment api structur review e g x submodul under the 140 0 mileston\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"0740d1ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"id\": \"90d5b7d4e0b671cc\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33858642536356726, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1617769362336675, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7511419, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"0740d1ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 3959, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:18\", \"token_count\": 1379, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- Add OTLP `insecure` support for logs to align with traces/metrics.\\n\\n- Continue supporting env-var config despite lack of formal spec guarantees.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-07]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-26\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3581463689  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-26T14:02:28Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-26T16:36:01Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-11-20  \\n\\n## Action Items\\n\\n- [ ] **Alex Boten**: Open issue to track evaluation of experimental API structure for the OTelConf RC module; add to `1.40` milestone.\\n\\n- [ ] **SIG reviewers**: Review the OTelConf RC support PR.\\n\\n- [ ] **Go approvers (not Tyler/David)**: Review PRs for sync-map histograms and exemplar reservoir.\\n\\n- [ ] **Contributors**: Review prototype for new attribute value types and limits.\\n\\n- [ ] **Tyler / spec contributors**: Consider raising follow-up spec issue for OTLP `insecure` behavior.\\n\\n- [ ] **Everyone**: Share notable KubeCon talks/videos in the channel.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"add otlp insecur support for log to align with trace metric continu support env var config despit lack of formal spec guarante sourc id src note 07 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 26 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3581463689 author pellar creat 2025 11 26t14 02 28z updat 2025 11 26t16 36 01z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 11 20 action item alex boten open issu to track evalu of experiment api structur for the otelconf rc modul add to 140 mileston sig review review the otelconf rc support pr go approv not tyler david review pr for sync map histogram and exemplar reservoir contributor review prototyp for new attribut valu type and limit tyler spec contributor consid rais follow up spec issu for otlp insecur behavior everyon share notabl kubecon talk video in the channel\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"0740d1ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"id\": \"1e4e5ba14876471d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30873635444720626, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12950033206743752, \"vector_similarity\": 0.72695374, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"0740d1ea8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 3959, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:18\", \"token_count\": 1379, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  - Group: Review and approve the PR.\\n\\n### 4) PR: Counter performance improvements; benchmarks and exemplar behavior\\n\\n- Summary:\\n\\n  - Significant optimization work on synchronous metric paths:\\n\\n    - Use sync.Map for attribute-set storage to improve read-heavy performance.\\n\\n    - Atomic sum values; “hot-cold” waitgroup technique to make measurements lockless and enable safe resets for delta aggregations (inspired by Prometheus histogram patterns).\\n\\n  - Known implications:\\n\\n    - Attribute-set limit becomes a soft limit due to race in attribute-set creation (map size tracking vs. map updates).\\n\\n    - For cumulative aggregations, enforcing attribute limits deterministically is harder since state persists; care needed to avoid inconsistent drops.\\n\\n    - Exemplar behavior: an Add may be included in the metric points but its exemplar may not be recorded in the same batch, which is acceptable and consistent with Prometheus and exemplar sampling design.\\n\\n- Discussion highlights:\\n\\n  - Potential follow-up: for exemplar reservoirs, a “merge” API could enable hot-cold reservoir consolidation for stricter atomicity at a higher level.\\n\\n  - Future performance work: histogram improvements and sharding (e.g., per-CPU) to reduce contention further.\\n\\n  - Benchmarks indicate substantial gains: ~10x for histograms with no contention; ~3x for fixed-size with shared contention.\\n\\n- Decisions:\\n\\n  - Accept current approach; exemplar variability is acceptable under spec/practice.\\n\\n  - Prioritize reviews for the benchmark PR and counter performance PR; histograms/fixed-size follow after.\\n\\n- Action items:\\n\\n  - David:\\n\\n    - Finalize and sequence PRs: benchmark fix (includes bug fix), counter performance improvements, then histogram/fixed-size improvements.\\n\\n    - Document soft-limit behavior and any mitigation for cumulative aggregations.\\n\\n  - Tyler/Group: Review benchmark PR and counter performance PR first; provide feedback and approvals.\\n\\n  - Tyler: Consider options to tie map-size accounting to updates more atomically; follow up with comments/ideas.\\n\\n## Decisions (summary)\\n\\n- Ownership and ops first: Establish clear owner, access, notifications, and playbooks for go.opentelemetry.io; explore migration to Netlify/Hugo only with owners’ approval.\\n\\n- Scope naming: Use instrumentation library name per spec; later add an attribute for the instrumented component/package (track via semantic conventions).\\n\\n- Error types: Adopt domain-specific error.type where available; proceed after GoDoc verification.\\n\\n- Performance work: Accept exemplar sampling variability; proceed with benchmark and counter performance PRs; histograms/fixed-size next.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"group review and approv the 